[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, entirely different.

389
00:19:17,005 --> 00:19:19,687
[SPEAKER_00]: What technique did he use?

390
00:19:19,987 --> 00:19:21,848
[SPEAKER_00]: Here's Hornsby, the difference between Hornsby and him.

391
00:19:22,228 --> 00:19:24,750
[SPEAKER_00]: Hornsby, as soon as he got in the clubhouse, he was under tension.

392
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:30,273
[SPEAKER_00]: You couldn't smoke, you couldn't read newspapers, you couldn't do nothing when you got in that clubhouse.

393
00:19:30,293 --> 00:19:36,096
[SPEAKER_00]: You never lost a ball in a clubhouse, never lost a ball game in a clubhouse, but you was under tension at all times.

394
00:19:36,677 --> 00:19:37,037
[SPEAKER_00]: Dykes,

395
00:19:38,314 --> 00:19:41,816
[SPEAKER_00]: Luke Atherton would come in every day and go to his office and tell them, I don't think I can make it.

396
00:19:41,936 --> 00:19:42,857
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't think I can make it.

397
00:19:42,877 --> 00:19:44,277
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why they call them aches and pains.

398
00:19:44,377 --> 00:19:46,179
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't think I'll be able to play today.

399
00:19:46,219 --> 00:19:51,982
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, and Dyke says to him, he says, you know, Luke, he says, someday, he says, you're really going to be sick.

400
00:19:52,022 --> 00:19:56,384
[SPEAKER_00]: And he says, nobody's going to believe you, and you're going to die.

401
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:57,225
[SPEAKER_00]: You always come in.

402
00:19:57,505 --> 00:19:59,986
[SPEAKER_00]: And you play cards and relax all the time.

403
00:20:00,006 --> 00:20:01,327
[SPEAKER_00]: He smoked a few cigars, probably.

404
00:20:01,407 --> 00:20:02,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, all the time, yeah.

405
00:20:02,708 --> 00:20:04,849
[SPEAKER_00]: Him and the pitcher.

406
00:20:07,151 --> 00:20:07,911
[SPEAKER_00]: Not the ball pitcher.

407
00:20:08,436 --> 00:20:15,761
[SPEAKER_00]: Ted Lyons, all the time sparring around, you know, half-dressed, you know, sparring around, knocking cigars out of one another's mouths.

408
00:20:16,182 --> 00:20:16,902
[SPEAKER_00]: And a lot of fun.

409
00:20:17,062 --> 00:20:18,303
[SPEAKER_00]: That's right.

410
00:20:18,743 --> 00:20:20,785
[SPEAKER_00]: And on the field, that's a horse of another color.

411
00:20:20,885 --> 00:20:22,386
[SPEAKER_00]: It was business.

412
00:20:22,406 --> 00:20:23,527
[SPEAKER_00]: It was all strictly business.

413
00:20:23,807 --> 00:20:25,728
[SPEAKER_01]: You think Dykes' method was best?

414
00:20:25,948 --> 00:20:26,989
[SPEAKER_00]: I thought so, yeah.

415
00:20:27,009 --> 00:20:27,910
[SPEAKER_00]: He was more relaxed.

416
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:29,251
[SPEAKER_00]: He managed longer in horseback.

417
00:20:29,271 --> 00:20:30,992
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yes, he did, yeah.

418
00:20:31,012 --> 00:20:32,433
[SPEAKER_00]: He went from place to place.

419
00:20:34,054 --> 00:20:36,356
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe great ballplayers don't make good men.

420
00:20:36,376 --> 00:20:36,876
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe they don't.

421
00:20:36,896 --> 00:20:37,797
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they're so good.

422
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:40,432
[SPEAKER_00]: And, you know, Rog liked to play the horses, too, you know.

423
00:20:41,593 --> 00:20:43,913
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes you'd see him in the morning, he wouldn't even speak to you, you know what I mean?

424
00:20:43,933 --> 00:20:45,773
[SPEAKER_00]: Like his mind was a blank or something like that.

425
00:20:46,653 --> 00:20:47,994
[SPEAKER_00]: We always said that's when he lost, you know.

426
00:20:48,014 --> 00:20:50,874
[SPEAKER_00]: And then when he was a lot of fun, well, that seems like that's when he won.

427
00:20:50,894 --> 00:20:51,674
[SPEAKER_01]: How'd he get away with this?

428
00:20:52,374 --> 00:20:53,155
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know.

429
00:20:53,175 --> 00:20:55,155
[SPEAKER_00]: I used to bet money for him.

430
00:20:55,415 --> 00:20:58,695
[SPEAKER_00]: When Spring Franklin was in West Palm Beach, he'd give me the money and I'd go bet on him.

431
00:20:59,416 --> 00:21:00,956
[SPEAKER_00]: He'd bet a hundred bucks, I'd bet a buck.

432
00:21:03,376 --> 00:21:06,517
[SPEAKER_00]: But some of his horses come in second and third, he's always betting them on the nose.

433
00:21:06,577 --> 00:21:07,857
[SPEAKER_00]: I'd bet a dollar across the board.

434
00:21:09,189 --> 00:21:11,611
[SPEAKER_00]: But that was his hobby, I guess.

435
00:21:11,631 --> 00:21:13,312
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course, that kept him broke, I guess.

436
00:21:14,754 --> 00:21:16,555
[SPEAKER_00]: But on the ball field, he was rough.

437
00:21:16,895 --> 00:21:18,717
[SPEAKER_01]: Who were some of your teammates with the Browns?

438
00:21:18,877 --> 00:21:19,538
[SPEAKER_00]: With the Browns?

439
00:21:19,898 --> 00:21:23,621
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, Harlan Cliff was one of them, yeah.

440
00:21:24,342 --> 00:21:26,023
[SPEAKER_00]: And Sammy West was another one.

441
00:21:26,063 --> 00:21:27,004
[SPEAKER_00]: He played center field.

442
00:21:28,145 --> 00:21:31,728
[SPEAKER_00]: And Hobo Hemsley, if you recall, Raleigh Hemsley, he was our catcher.

443
00:21:32,348 --> 00:21:34,590
[SPEAKER_01]: Tell me a little bit about Hemsley, his private life.

444
00:21:34,610 --> 00:21:37,072
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, he was a character.

445
00:21:37,132 --> 00:21:37,713
[SPEAKER_00]: He and I,

446
00:21:39,007 --> 00:21:45,051
[SPEAKER_00]: Went to Philadelphia, we were in Philadelphia, and went out for the evening, we had a few beers, we went different places.

447
00:21:45,532 --> 00:21:48,434
[SPEAKER_00]: We come home about quarter to twelve, they were checking us in, you know.

448
00:21:49,074 --> 00:21:52,937
[SPEAKER_00]: Next morning I get up and read the paper for breakfast at nine o'clock, and here's Henry's in jail.

449
00:21:53,217 --> 00:21:54,598
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, how did they get in jail?

450
00:21:55,139 --> 00:21:56,460
[SPEAKER_00]: He went, he come home with me, see.

451
00:21:57,460 --> 00:22:07,708
[SPEAKER_00]: So he got out that night, he went out the back fire escape there somewhere, got out, went and got himself a rental car or something, and he didn't have a Pennsylvania driver's license, didn't have no driver's license at all I guess,

452
00:22:08,353 --> 00:22:14,579
[SPEAKER_00]: He got himself jacked up a little bit, I guess, and he got into a spot where there was a bunch of Navy boys, and they worked him over a little bit.

453
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,903
[SPEAKER_00]: And I still don't know how he got out, but he got out.

454
00:22:19,563 --> 00:22:20,584
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how he told me he got out.

455
00:22:21,865 --> 00:22:24,287
[SPEAKER_00]: And the times that he caught, I couldn't understand how he caught.

456
00:22:24,347 --> 00:22:26,710
[SPEAKER_00]: And he says, well, by the third or fourth, he'd sweat out, you know.

457
00:22:27,710 --> 00:22:29,452
[SPEAKER_00]: And, of course, it was all day ball in those days, you know.

458
00:22:29,972 --> 00:22:32,795
[SPEAKER_00]: But I never saw the man drunk myself, to tell you the truth.

459
00:22:34,407 --> 00:22:35,888
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you say checked in?

460
00:22:35,908 --> 00:22:36,969
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you have a bed check?

461
00:22:37,069 --> 00:22:38,791
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yes, at midnight.

462
00:22:38,831 --> 00:22:39,451
[SPEAKER_01]: What was this?

463
00:22:39,471 --> 00:22:40,272
[SPEAKER_01]: With the Browns?

464
00:22:40,612 --> 00:22:41,893
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, with the St. Louis Browns, yeah.

465
00:22:41,913 --> 00:22:42,714
[SPEAKER_01]: Barnsby do this?

466
00:22:42,954 --> 00:22:43,755
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yeah, oh yeah.

467
00:22:43,915 --> 00:22:45,176
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, all big leagues had that.

468
00:22:45,336 --> 00:22:50,520
