477
00:23:16,334 --> 00:23:18,855
[SPEAKER_00]: And Tony Kubik's father, you remember Tony Kubik?

478
00:23:18,955 --> 00:23:23,939
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, Tony Kubik's father, he was Milwaukee, and Jack Cloza, they joined us that day.

479
00:23:23,979 --> 00:23:29,822
[SPEAKER_00]: Jack Cloza had two triples, only two hits a got, about 13, 14 times at bat, and both of them won the ball game, I'll never forget that.

480
00:23:30,703 --> 00:23:32,284
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I played ball with Tony Kubik's dad.

481
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:34,501
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, his name was Tony, too.

482
00:23:34,661 --> 00:23:35,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, he played ball.

483
00:23:36,983 --> 00:23:40,825
[SPEAKER_00]: He never got in the big leagues, but he played, well, his home was Milwaukee, too.

484
00:23:41,625 --> 00:23:42,606
[SPEAKER_00]: Jim Levy with you?

485
00:23:43,326 --> 00:23:44,727
[SPEAKER_00]: No, Jim was there ahead of me.

486
00:23:45,168 --> 00:23:46,268
[SPEAKER_00]: Jim was there ahead of me, yeah.

487
00:23:47,129 --> 00:23:48,129
[SPEAKER_00]: And Sammy West.

488
00:23:48,550 --> 00:23:51,331
[SPEAKER_00]: Then we had Moose Saunders.

