00:26:02,979 --> 00:26:07,741
[SPEAKER_00]: Unknowingly, you know, the guy, the pitcher goes into a wind-up, you know, and what's he doing winding up?

530
00:26:07,761 --> 00:26:08,821
[SPEAKER_00]: So you're taking off, right?

531
00:26:09,701 --> 00:26:11,042
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't know the guy's on third.

532
00:26:11,062 --> 00:26:15,723
[SPEAKER_00]: You figure, geez, if I can go from home to second, he should go from second to home when the ball's thrown in the right field.

533
00:26:16,183 --> 00:26:19,464
[SPEAKER_00]: But he probably, after the ball was fielded, he probably went back to second, you know.

534
00:26:20,064 --> 00:26:22,245
[SPEAKER_00]: Thinking they're going to, you know, pick him off or something.

535
00:26:22,673 --> 00:26:27,095
