536
00:26:27,455 --> 00:26:29,656
[SPEAKER_00]: But here I'm running and I thought the guy scored, see.

537
00:26:30,036 --> 00:26:33,777
[SPEAKER_00]: As the pitcher goes into his lineup and I'm taking off and what's he lining up for, I'm taking off.

538
00:26:35,358 --> 00:26:37,679
[SPEAKER_00]: But that only happens once, you know, that's how you learn.

539
00:26:37,959 --> 00:26:39,199
[SPEAKER_00]: I've seen it happen several times.

540
00:26:39,219 --> 00:26:41,160
[SPEAKER_00]: Hard to say about that.

541
00:26:43,041 --> 00:26:49,123
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, get out of here for making mistakes, mental mistakes more for the mechanical, you know what I mean.

542
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:54,257
[SPEAKER_00]: If you do the wrong thing, like you run on a fly ball, you say, what you doing running on a fly ball?

543
00:26:54,277 --> 00:26:55,618
[SPEAKER_00]: I thought it was two outs.

544
00:26:55,938 --> 00:26:57,319
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't think, I'll do the thinking.

545
00:26:58,980 --> 00:27:01,802
[SPEAKER_00]: Because by errors like this, we drop the ball.

546
00:27:01,902 --> 00:27:06,466
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the only, anybody that played the game knows he dropped balls, or he threw balls away, or he kicked balls away.

547
00:27:07,387 --> 00:27:11,090
[SPEAKER_00]: But mental error, that means your mind isn't on the game or something, you know.

548
00:27:12,251 --> 00:27:15,273
