562
00:27:53,780 --> 00:27:56,961
[SPEAKER_00]: That was 19, 1933, 32, somewhere in there, see.

563
00:27:57,942 --> 00:28:02,744
[SPEAKER_00]: And he got a home run because his ball landed before the second baseman around got the ball.

564
00:28:02,784 --> 00:28:03,745
[SPEAKER_00]: Pitt ran all the way around.

565
00:28:05,065 --> 00:28:08,267
[SPEAKER_00]: That was the most sorriest thing I ever saw because they carried them both off on stretchers.

566
00:28:11,655 --> 00:28:16,357
[SPEAKER_00]: Some of the funny things, you have to stop and think some of the funny things that have happened, you know.

567
00:28:16,377 --> 00:28:20,898
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, old ball players talking, you used to hear some of the craziest stories.

568
00:28:20,918 --> 00:28:21,559
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, that's the truth.

569
00:28:21,719 --> 00:28:22,319
[SPEAKER_01]: Wonderful.

570
00:28:22,339 --> 00:28:22,859
[SPEAKER_01]: That's right.

571
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:24,800
[SPEAKER_01]: It must be a...

572
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,200
[SPEAKER_00]: It was quite a career.

